he Naturalist&#39;s turn, The Naturalist regains 1 HP.&quot; The other has the Purple Rhino effect &quot;At the start of Guise&#39;s turn, Guise regains 1 HP.&quot; Both of them can activate Purple Rhino effects. So, at the start of The Naturalist&#39;s turn, one Purple Rhino effect triggers. Can they both activate it? If so, (b) happens since both trigger since both players are triggering the text on The Naturalist&#39;s version. If not, then (a) happens. Then, can Guise activate his version of the purple rhino effect at the start of The Naturalist&#39;s turn? I&#39;d expect no, but if so, then (c) would trigger. And then, the converse. If (a) happens, I&#39;d expect (d) to happen, same with (b) and (e), and (c) and (f).</span></p><p>EDIT: To reword this last one, I can only see three valid outcomes here&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">&nbsp;(all assuming Resilient Hide was played prior to &quot;Uh, Yeah, I&#39;m That Guy&quot;)</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">:</span></p><p>(A) At the start of&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">The Naturalist&#39;s turn, The Naturalist regains 1 HP. At the start of Guise&#39;s turn, Guise regains 1 HP.</span></p><p>(B) At the start of The Naturalist&#39;s turn, The Naturalist regains 1 HP, then The Naturalist regains 1 HP. At the start of Guise&#39;s turn, Guise regains 1 HP, then Guise regains 1 HP.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">(C) At the start of The Naturalist&#39;s turn, The Naturalist regains 1 HP, then Guise regains 1 HP. At the start of Guise&#39;s turn, The Naturalist regains 1 HP, then&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Guise regains 1 HP.</span></p>",
